6	//
7	// Every layer here is the real one. The relay is the actual `notify-relay` crate running its
8	// real accept loop, store, and APNs client in-process; the transport is real QUIC over
9	// loopback; the seal is real HPKE. Only Apple is a stand-in, because Apple is the one party
10	// we cannot run.
11	//
12	// This is what the per-layer tests cannot cover: each side's unit tests prove it is
13	// self-consistent, and this proves the two sides agree — the envelope Custos builds is the
14	// envelope the relay serializes, the padding budget Custos computed is the length Apple
15	// actually sees, and the payload a device receives opens under the key the instance
16	// published. A wire drift between the crates fails here and nowhere else.
17	
18	#![cfg(test)]
